{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "label": "DevTools", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_attach", "label": "DevTools.attach", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Binds a server of its own, which is usually what you want since the DevTools port should be firewalled separately from the application port. Detach happens automatically during CoordinatedShutdown, so a SIGTERM releases the port."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_mount", "label": "DevTools.mount", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unlike attach it never learns where its routes end up - host is not read on this path - so DevTools cannot tell a private port from a public one and will not guess. It therefore asks for the gate up front, and auth or ipAllowlist wrap the returned tree so the gate travels with it wherever it is mounted."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtoolsoptions", "label": "DevToolsOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security_posture", "label": "DevTools security posture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DevTools is a debugger and the defaults treat it as one: loopback by default, a routable bind must be deliberate (auth, ipAllowlist or allowRemote, with the error naming all three so a typo in a host string cannot quietly publish actor state), a mount must acknowledge its gate, and gates wrap the UI, the JSON endpoints and the WebSocket upgrade alike because a gate on only the JSON would leave the actual data channel open."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_same_origin_sockets", "label": "Same-origin WebSocket rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tap accepts an upgrade whose Origin names the tap itself and rejects any other, so a page you visit cannot dial your local DevTools. A request with no Origin is allowed because CSWSH needs a browser and a browser always sends one. Binding to loopback is not a substitute: a WebSocket handshake is not subject to the same-origin policy, so any page in the developer browser can reach 127.0.0.1."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panel_switches", "label": "Per-panel switches", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A disabled panel is disabled for good - its control methods are never registered, so its data never leaves the process whatever a client asks for. Time travel is the one to think about first because it surfaces raw persisted events."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_metrics_registry_auto_enable", "label": "Metrics registry auto-enable while attached", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Message throughput, mailbox drops and handler latency are counted by the framework itself and read 0 against the default noop registry, so DevTools switches the registry on at attach and puts the noop back on detach. A registry you enabled yourself is left alone in both directions."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_cluster_connection_trust", "label": "Cluster readings trust the connection, not the message", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A node replies down the connection the question arrived on, never to an address the question named, and the collector files a reading under the address the transport supplied, never the one the reading claims for itself. Only a current member gets a row, and both row count and reported tree size are capped - so a peer that lies can only lie about its own row. This is not authentication of the cluster port; that is mTLS."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_example_devtools_wiring", "label": "DevTools wiring in the examples", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only examples that run until you stop them are wired. An example that finishes on its own carries no reference to DevTools at all, so it can be copied into a project and run unchanged. Seven cluster and management examples had only ever attached, binding a port and logging a URL that was dead before a browser could open it; teaching them to stay up would have handed the browser an already-gone system or deleted the teardown that is the demonstration."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_no_node_reachable_dialog", "label": "No node reachable dialog", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every panel keeps showing the last thing it was told, so a lost connection would otherwise look exactly like a healthy system. The dialog names it and counts how long it has been true, the panel stays dimmed, and the uptime counter freezes rather than counting up past the death of the system it measures."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_ui_build", "label": "DevTools UI build", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vanilla TypeScript bundled by Bun.build and embedded into the published package, so it needs no UI framework at runtime and no network access; uiDevelopmentRoot serves it from disk for panel development."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_port_counting", "label": "DevTools port counting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each attachment takes its own port counting up from the configured base, per process - so a cluster built from separate terminals takes the first free port in the range the way the cluster transport scans for its own. If none is free, or anything else about DevTools fails, the example logs a warning and starts anyway: a debugger that cannot bind is not a reason for the program under debug to die."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_attach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_mount", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtoolsoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security_posture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_same_origin_sockets", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panel_switches", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_metrics_registry_auto_enable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_cluster_connection_trust", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_example_devtools_wiring", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_no_node_reachable_dialog", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_ui_build", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source